ntors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IRIE TADASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITANI HIKARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHITANI YASUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IRIE, TADASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITANI, HIKARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHITANI, YASUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Cephem compounds represented by general formula (I) which have a broad antibacterial spectrum over various pathogenic bacteria and are also efficacious against MRSA, wherein X represents N or CY (wherein Y represents H or halogeno); R&lt;1&gt; represents optionally protected amino; R&lt;2&gt; represents hydrogen, optionally substituted lower alkyl, etc.; R&lt;3&gt; represents hydrogen, etc.; R&lt;4&gt; represents hydrogen, optionally substituted lower alkyl, an optionally substituted nitrogen-containing heterocycle, etc.; R&lt;5&gt; represents hydrogen, etc.; and the wavy lines means syn- or anti-isomerism or a mixture thereof.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne des composés de céphème représentés par la formule générale (I) et présentant un large spectre antibactérien agissant sur diverses bactéries pathogènes, tout en étant efficaces contre le staphylocoque doré résistant à la méthicilline. Dans cette formule, X est N ou CY, Y étant H ou halogéno. R&lt;1&gt; est amino éventuellement protégé. R&lt;2&gt; est hydrogène, alkyle inférieur éventuellement substitué, etc. R&lt;3&gt; est hydrogène, etc. R&lt;4&gt; est hydrogène, alkyle inférieur éventuellement substitué, hétérocycle azoté éventuellement substitué, etc. R&lt;5&gt; est hydrogène, etc. et les liaisons en lignes brisées signifie synisomérisme ou anti-isomérisme, ou un mélange des deux.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>